[2.0] WHAT THIS IS
------------------
This is a x most popular/most downloaded files bulletin maker for
Zeus Proffesional BBS. It also writes some extra stats. The output
looks just like PopFile's, a ABBS bulletin maker by NHSW/Tor W.
Austerslått.


[2.1] QUICK INTRODUCTION
------------------------
Type the following line in a CLI/SHELL:

ZTopFiles "RAM:TopFiles.txt" BBS "CeCom"


[2.2] REQUIREMENTS
------------------
In order to use this program you need:

   o An Amiga compatible computer with AmigaDOS 2.04, or higher,
     installed.

   o Zeus Proffesional BBS and file server must be running.


[2.3] FEATURES
--------------
   o Number of files in list is configurable.

   o Using ReadArgs().

   o Can be made resident.

   o Which areas to scan is configurable.

   o Unvalidated files can be included in the list.

   o Nice ANSI output.


[2.4] INSTALLATION
------------------
Copy it anywhere, e.g. ZEUS:Doors/.


[2.5] USAGE
-----------
FILE/A,BBSNAME=BBS/K/A,FILES=F/N/K,AREAS=A/K,UNVALIDATED=UNVAL/S:

FILE.......: Full path to a file to write the bulletin.
BBSNAME....: The name of your BBS.
FILES......: Number of files to include in the list.
AREAS......: Areas and/or ranges of areas to scan. E.g.
             "1-10,15,100-150"
UNVALIDATED: Include unvalidated files in list.


